DRIFTCORE SAFETY COPYLEFT LICENSE (DSCL)
Version 0.1 — DRAFT FOR LEGAL REVIEW

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
⚠️  IMPORTANT NOTICE — READ FIRST
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

THIS IS A DRAFT. It has not been reviewed by a lawyer.
It has not been tested in any court. Do not rely on it as
legal protection until it has been professionally reviewed.

It exists to capture INTENT clearly, so a qualified attorney
can convert that intent into enforceable legal language.

Recommended legal review resources:
  - Software Freedom Conservancy (sfconservancy.org)
  - Open Source Initiative (opensource.org)
  - Hippocratic License project (firstdonoharm.dev)
  - RAIL Licenses initiative (licenses.ai)

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
PLAIN LANGUAGE SUMMARY — FOR EVERYONE
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

What you CAN do:
  ✅ Use DriftCore for free, forever, for any safe purpose
  ✅ Use it commercially — build businesses on it
  ✅ Modify it, improve it, extend it
  ✅ Distribute it and your modifications
  ✅ ADD new safety invariants and protections

What you MUST do:
  📌 Keep derivatives open source (copyleft)
  📌 Preserve ALL safety invariants in any derivative
  📌 Preserve the transparency layer (Fable) in any derivative
  📌 Preserve human-in-loop requirements in any derivative
  📌 Credit the project and document your changes

What you CANNOT do:
  ❌ Remove or weaken any safety invariant
  ❌ Use it in autonomous weapons systems
  ❌ Use it for autonomous lethal decision-making
  ❌ Use it to remove human oversight from consequential decisions
  ❌ Lock it inside hardware that users cannot inspect or modify
  ❌ Make the software deceive its human operators

The core idea — SAFETY COPYLEFT:
  GPL made software freedom viral: free software stays free.
  This license makes safety viral: safe software stays safe.
  Invariants can be ADDED in derivatives. Never REMOVED.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
THE LICENSE
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

SECTION 1 — DEFINITIONS

1.1 "The Software" means DriftCore OS, including all source
    code, documentation, and associated files distributed
    under this license.

1.2 "Derivative Work" means any work based on or incorporating
    the Software, in whole or in part, whether modified or not.

1.3 "Safety Invariants" means the immutable constraints defined
    in the file driftcore/kernel/invariants.py, including but
    not limited to:
      (a) NO_AUTONOMOUS_LETHAL_DECISION
      (b) NO_WEAPONS_DESIGN
      (c) NO_ATTACK_PLANNING
      (d) NO_AUTONOMOUS_TARGETING
      (e) HUMAN_OVERSIGHT_CANNOT_BE_DISABLED
      (f) AUDIT_CHAIN_CANNOT_BE_DELETED
      (g) SAFETY_KERNEL_CANNOT_BE_WEAKENED
      (h) NO_SELF_MODIFICATION_OF_SAFETY_RULES
      (i) NO_DECEPTION_OF_HUMAN_OPERATORS

1.4 "Transparency Layer" means the Fable subsystem providing
    human-readable narration and immutable audit records.

1.5 "Autonomous Weapons System" means any system capable of
    selecting and engaging targets, or applying force intended
    to harm, disable, or kill, without an individual human
    authorization for each such action at the moment of action.

1.6 "Consequential Decision" means any decision that may
    materially affect a person's life, health, liberty,
    livelihood, or legal rights.


SECTION 2 — GRANT OF RIGHTS

2.1 Subject to the conditions of this license, you are granted
    a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, perpetual license
    to use, copy, modify, and distribute the Software and
    Derivative Works, for any purpose not prohibited by
    Section 4.

2.2 PATENT GRANT (adapted from Apache 2.0): Each contributor
    grants you a perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free patent
    license covering their contributions. If you initiate
    patent litigation against any entity alleging the Software
    infringes a patent, your rights under this license
    terminate immediately.


SECTION 3 — SAFETY COPYLEFT CONDITIONS

3.1 OPEN DERIVATIVES (adapted from GPL v3): Any Derivative
    Work that you distribute must be licensed under this same
    license, with complete corresponding source code made
    available.

3.2 INVARIANT PRESERVATION (original to this license):
    Any Derivative Work MUST preserve all Safety Invariants
    in full force and effect. Derivative Works MAY add new
    Safety Invariants. Derivative Works MAY NOT remove,
    weaken, disable, or circumvent any existing Safety
    Invariant.

    A Derivative Work that removes or weakens any Safety
    Invariant is NOT licensed under this license, and its
    distribution constitutes copyright infringement.

3.3 TRANSPARENCY PRESERVATION: Any Derivative Work must
    preserve the Transparency Layer or a functional equivalent
    providing: (a) human-readable narration of safety events,
    and (b) tamper-evident audit records that operators
    cannot delete.

3.4 ANTI-TIVOIZATION (adapted from GPL v3): If you distribute
    the Software embedded in hardware, you must provide users
    the information and means necessary to inspect, modify,
    and reinstall modified versions of the Software on that
    hardware, except where doing so is prohibited by
    applicable safety certification law.

3.5 ATTRIBUTION: You must retain all copyright notices,
    this license text, and a prominent notice of any changes
    you made.


SECTION 4 — PROHIBITED USES

The rights granted in Section 2 do NOT extend to, and this
license is automatically void for, any of the following uses:

4.1 Use in, or integration with, any Autonomous Weapons System.

4.2 Use for autonomous lethal decision-making of any kind.

4.3 Use to identify, select, prioritize, or track human targets
    for any harmful action.

4.4 Use to design, optimize, or improve weapons, munitions,
    or systems whose primary purpose is to cause harm.

4.5 Use that removes human oversight from Consequential
    Decisions.

4.6 Use to deceive the human operators of the system about
    the system's state, actions, or capabilities.

4.7 Use in violation of the Universal Declaration of Human
    Rights or applicable international humanitarian law.

PERMITTED DEFENSIVE USES — for the avoidance of doubt, the
following are NOT prohibited:
  - Threat detection that alerts human operators
  - Protective shutdown of dangerous systems
  - Audit and accountability infrastructure
  - Human-in-loop enforcement added to existing systems


SECTION 5 — TERMINATION

5.1 Your rights under this license terminate automatically
    upon any violation of Sections 3 or 4.

5.2 Rights may be reinstated if the violation is cured within
    30 days of notice, unless the violation involved
    Section 4 (Prohibited Uses), in which case termination
    is permanent.


SECTION 6 — DISCLAIMER OF WARRANTY

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY
KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO
WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR
PURPOSE, AND NONINFRINGEMENT.

THE SOFTWARE IS A SAFETY FRAMEWORK BUT IS NOT CERTIFIED
SAFETY EQUIPMENT. IT HAS NOT BEEN CERTIFIED UNDER IEC 61508,
ISO 13849, ISO 26262, OR ANY OTHER FUNCTIONAL SAFETY
STANDARD. DO NOT RELY ON IT AS THE SOLE PROTECTION FOR
LIFE-SAFETY APPLICATIONS. ALWAYS USE CERTIFIED HARDWARE
INTERLOCKS FOR LIFE-SAFETY FUNCTIONS.


SECTION 7 — LIMITATION OF LIABILITY

IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS, CONTRIBUTORS, OR COPYRIGHT
HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES, OR OTHER LIABILITY,
WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT, OR OTHERWISE, ARISING
FROM, OUT OF, OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE
OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.


SECTION 8 — INTERPRETATION

8.1 If any provision of this license is held unenforceable,
    the remaining provisions remain in full effect, and the
    unenforceable provision shall be reformed to the minimum
    extent necessary to make it enforceable while preserving
    its intent.

8.2 The Plain Language Summary above is provided for
    accessibility. In case of conflict, the numbered sections
    govern.

